Package: korealocalelection2022
Title: Province-Level Analysis of South Korea's 2022 Local Elections
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jumin", "Cho", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tidy, documented province-level results of South Korea's 7th
    (2018) and 8th (2022) nationwide local elections and the 20th
    presidential election (2022), simplified province boundaries, and the R
    code that validates the data and reproduces every figure and statistic in
    the README. This is an analysis project, not an installable package; the
    file declares its dependencies so that remotes::install_deps() can set up
    an environment.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/jumincho/korea-local-election-2022
BugReports: https://github.com/jumincho/korea-local-election-2022/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    dplyr (>= 1.1.0),
    ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0),
    ggrepel,
    here,
    patchwork,
    ragg,
    readr (>= 2.0.0),
    scales,
    sf (>= 1.0-10),
    tidyr (>= 1.3.0)
Suggests:
    lintr (>= 3.0.0),
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
